{"resourceIdentifier":"316","resourceName":"PARAMONGA BAGASSE BOILER PROJECT","description":"Agro Industrial Paramonga S.A. - AIPSA, is one of the largest sugar companies in Peru, producing approximately 110 thousand metric tonnes of sugar annually, which represents an 11% share of the total national sugar production. AIPSA‘s steam requirements were produced by the boilers using Bunker fuel, complemented by residual pith and bagasse as fuel inputs.  The objective of the project activity is to generate the financial resources necessary to finance the reconversion of the energy generation system of AIPSA, from the Residual Fuel Oil based energy generation system, to a new energy system based on biomass residues. The project activity contributes to sustainable development because it displaces a fossil fuel system with a biomass based renewable energy system, generating benefits not only by reducing greenhouse gases, but by also reducing other local air pollutants and environmental impacts associated with the burning of Bunker fuel which have deteriorated the local environment.","location":{"latitude":-10.672222,"longitude":-77.816667},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"316"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AGRO INDUSTRIAL PARAMONGA SAA"},{"type":"string","value":"LIMA, Peru"},{"type":"string","value":"511 202 1111"},{"type":"string","value":"ewong@agroparamonga.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"316"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"123136"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Energy industries (renewable/non-renewable sources)"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AM0036"}]